  "notes": "Two-page piano piece on ONE grand staff. A correct conversion yields exactly ONE part \"Piano\" (2 staves, 24 bars, measures continue across the page turn); the held lower right-hand voice in the variation (bars 13-24) is voice 2 of the piano part, not a separate part. DAMAGE (stain-pencil): Rehearsal copy: coffee ring stains (scan: one ring over the music), graphite pencil marks - circled notes, handwritten words (\"rit.\", \"breathe\", \"p\", \"cresc.\" ...), breath ticks/commas, arrows, phrase arcs, fingering digits above notes. Severe adds three stains, yellow and pink highlighter over staff passages, blue ballpoint circles/words and margin scribbles. Exact positions of every mark are listed per file in meta.annotations. TRUTH LIMITATIONS: Handwritten marks (including handwritten dynamics such as \"p\", \"mf\", \"cresc.\", \"rit.\" and fingerings) are NOT in the truth: the truth only contains the engraved music. A conversion that adds them as dynamics/words/fingerings is wrong for scoring purposes."
